cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use rete, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "rete: browser-native SPARQL over static, range-addressable RDF files"
abstract: >-
  rete is a cloud-native, range-queryable RDF graph file format and engine. A
  `.rete` file is a single immutable artifact that answers SPARQL by HTTP range
  reads, so a multi-gigabyte graph is queryable from static hosting — in the
  browser, from the CLI, or from Python, JavaScript, R, Java and Blender — with
  no server and no database. An embedded Dataset Card makes each file
  self-describing in two small range requests at any size.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Vivar Rios"
    given-names: "Carlos"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8076-2034"
    email: "carlos.vivarrios@epfl.ch"
repository-code: "https://github.com/caviri/rete"
url: "https://caviri.github.io/rete/"
license: Apache-2.0
# Concept DOI (Zenodo `conceptdoi`, parent record 21546287): resolves to the
# latest archived release rather than pinning one. Never the per-version DOI —
# 10.5281/zenodo.21546288 is v0.3.0's and would freeze every citation there.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21546287"
keywords:
  - RDF
  - SPARQL
  - knowledge graph
  - linked data
  - file format
  - range requests
  - WebAssembly
  - serverless
